Agreed: the prior plan was too much for the next slice.

Drafted the minimal-code alternative:

`docs/plan/2026-06-09/02.prost-bytes-dsa-minimal-code.draft.md`

Core idea:
- no Prost derive changes;
- no `TransferMessage`;
- no Tonic async/pending buffer changes;
- add a DSA-aware `BufMut` wrapper in `tonic-dsa-bytes-sync`;
- pass it to normal `prost::Message::encode`;
- override only `BufMut::put<T: Buf>` so large protobuf `bytes` payload copies can use synchronous DSA;
- keep strings/scalars/varints on CPU.

This is a better first measurement gate: if sync DSA inside Prost’s existing write path is not promising, the larger async field-aware design is not worth building.

